ng sports over academics – was true, it doesn't mean the *innate capacity* of those athletes was lower. This was more of a cultural problem than any sort of genetic thing. Finally, I want to bring it back to the cousin. Recognizing this generational belief means the cousin will likely be walking into an environment with a lot of historical baggage. Some people, including teachers, might judge him based on this long-standing stereotype. He needs to be prepared for that.
